{"name":"Quartzite","hex":"#232e26","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quartzite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metamorphic rock from sandstone, consisting of interlocking grains of quartz."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quartzite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quartzite","blocks":[{"text":"Quartzite is a hard, non-foliated metamorphic rock that was originally pure quartz sandstone. Sandstone is converted into quartzite through heating and pressure usually related to tectonic compression within orogenic belts, and hence quartzite is a metasandstone. Pure quartzite is usually white to grey, though quartzites often occur in various shades of pink and red due to varying amounts of hematite. Other colors, such as yellow, green, blue and orange, are due to other minerals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Quartzite_Solli%C3%A8res.jpg/330px-Quartzite_Solli%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartzite","wikidata":"Q237883"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG/500px-Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG/1280px-Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG/500px-Sample_of_Quartzite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Quartzite can have a grainy, glassy, sandpaper-like surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASample_of_Quartzite.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Quartzite_Mine_in_Kakwa_Park.JPG/500px-Quartzite_Mine_in_Kakwa_Park.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa